## Putting It All Together: A Mini‑Demo

```rust
#[derive(Debug)]
enum Status {
    Ok(i32),            // success, carries an ID
    Err(String),        // failure, carries a message
    Pending,            // no data
}

fn main() {
    let response = Status::Ok(42);
    // Pattern match
    match response {
        Status::Ok(id) => println!("Success! ID = {}", id),
        Status::Err(msg) => eprintln!("Error: {}", msg),
        Status::Pending => println!("Still pending…"),
    }

    // if let for a quick check
    if let Status::Ok(id) = response {
        println!("We got an ID: {}", id);
    }

    // while let – pop until empty
    let mut vec = vec![Status::Ok(1), Status::Pending, Status::Err("oops".into())];
    while let Some(s) = vec.pop() {
        println!("Processing: {:?}", s);
    }
}
```

Output:

```
Success! ID = 42
We got an ID: 42
Processing: Err("oops")
Processing: Pending
Processing: Ok(1)
```

