## Why Use Enums + Pattern Matching?

| Reason | What it gives you |
|--------|-------------------|
| **Type safety** | The compiler knows all possible variants; you can’t accidentally miss a case. |
| **Expressiveness** | A single enum can encode a whole protocol or set of states. |
| **Concise code** | `match`, `if let`, and `while let` let you work directly with the data. |
| **No runtime “type‑casts”** | The tag is checked at compile‑time, so no unchecked casts or reflection. |

That’s the core of Rust’s enum + pattern matching idiom: a powerful, safe, and
concise way to model “one of many” data shapes and to react to them. Happy
pattern‑matching!
